                                                "text": "the Proteus Principle helps to qualify and balance the concepts of narrators and of narrative situations as previously developed in classical studies by G erard Genette and Franz Stanzel."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2202865a-4275-31d6-a4d5-c99041b1588b",
                                        "entry_id": "1d99375d-fb2a-337d-be24-a066e2434c9a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To hold (an object or objects) precariously; to support on a narrow base, so as to keep from falling."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "930b6f8d-e73a-455a-a90f-6e08f6db8742",
                                                "sense_id": "2202865a-4275-31d6-a4d5-c99041b1588b",
                                                "text": "I balanced my mug of coffee on my knee."
                                            },
